<title>PERU: Peru's May coffee output rises 9.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's May coffee output rises 9.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's May coffee production increased 9.5 percent to 33,513 tonnes, from 30,617 tonnes in the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>Five-month output, however, was off 2.1 percent to 56,703 tonnes from 57,923 tonnes in the January-May period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Non-decaffeinated coffee exports in the first five months were $24.6 million, down from $32.6 million in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>((-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
